      "feedback": "The revisions directly address the highest-priority gaps and elevate the entry to research-grade accuracy. Elevating Pouteria campechiana to the primary heading aligns the record with USDA, UF/IFAS, and Flora of North America standards, while retaining Lucuma campechiana as the basionym in the notes demonstrates deep taxonomic nuance.\n\nReframing the frugivory from a negative (\"birds avoid it\") to a positive evolutionary narrative (\"mammal dispersal syndrome\") transforms a passive observation into an active ecological lesson—exactly the kind of insightful interpretation that distinguishes world-class botanical institutions. The added field marks (terminal spiral leaf clusters) and microclimate specifics (28–29°F tolerance limits for Zone 9b/10a) give both amateur plant enthusiasts and local landscapers practical, actionable field value.\n\nTo refine this page further before publication, consider these minor editorial adjustments:\n\nBloom & Harvest Phenology: Adding explicit seasonality for",
